.env
# Environment files other than `.env` itself: override files and pre-deploy
# snapshots (.env.override, .env.pre-<change>.<timestamp>). These are copies of
# a live environment and carry real values -- Neo4j password, paperclip tokens,
# the projection HMAC secret, the signing key, node tokens.
#
# `.env` alone was matched, so every one of those variants was untracked but NOT
# ignored, and a routine `git add -A` would have committed them. Per
# docs/SECURITY_SECRETS_AND_FLEET_IDENTITY_PLAN.md, secret values must never
# enter Git.
#
# `.env.example` stays trackable: it is the documented template, not a copy.
.env.*
!.env.example
deploy/canary.env
deploy/canary-*.env
deploy/reconciliation.env
deploy/reconciliation/migration-state.yaml
deploy/reconciliation/final-cutover-evidence.yaml
deploy/reconciliation/runtime-projection.yaml
deploy/reconciliation/lan-runtime-map.json
deploy/local/
artifacts/deployment-canary/
artifacts/reconciliation-preflight/
artifacts/reconciliation-render/
artifacts/reconciliation-images/
artifacts/reconciliation-hermes-home/
artifacts/reconciliation-tailnet-candidates.json
artifacts/reconciliation-tailnet-candidates.json.sha256
artifacts/runtime-projection-approval-evidence.json
artifacts/runtime-projection-evidence.json
artifacts/reconciliation-report*.md
.venv/
env/
venv/
__pycache__/
*.pyc

*.assistx_cache.sqlite
.assistx_cache.sqlite
